00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:21.240
Catalyst event investing focuses on specific news developments that can drive short-term price moves in a stock or sector.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:29.200
Today's AMD CEO meeting with Samsung's semiconductor head creates a potential partnership signal in the chip space.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:37.080
Investors can screen for such events by setting news alerts on major semiconductor names and checking volume on the announcement day.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:44.720
The approach works best when the catalyst aligns with broader sector momentum and volume confirmation above the 20-day average.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:51.700
risks include the meeting producing low concrete follow-through and broader market rotation pulling capital elsewhere.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:59.660
A practical implementation starts with a watch list of 10 chip stocks, adding any name that reports a high level executive meeting,

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.320
and confirming the volume spike before entry.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:10.180
Historical examples show these setups deliver the strongest results when the news arrives during an earning season with positive sector breadth.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:16.020
Always pair the catalyst with a clear invalidation level, such as no follow-up announcement within

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:16.760
30 days.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.780
The volume filter helps avoid entries where rotation pressure overrides the news.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:27.340
Sector rotation checks add another layer by confirming inflows into semi-conductors before

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:28.440
sizing the position.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:35.100
Imagine you already own a TFSA and want income exposure without managing tenants or mortgages

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:35.620
directly.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:41.620
Publicly traded reats, such as smart centers, issued to benches like the new $300 million

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:47.520
theories AE, at 4.795% to fund property operations.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:53.880
These vehicles trade on the TSX and distribute income monthly, while the trust handles property

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:55.100
management and leasing.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:01.080
Mortgage investment corporations offer another route by pooling loans secured against real estate

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.660
and paying out interest income that flows through to unit holders.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:10.120
measures. Rental property ownership requires direct capital and effort, but allows leverage

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:14.960
and potential capital gains treatment on sale. Tax treatment differs sharply.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:21.300
Reat distributions often count as return of capital, reducing adjusted cost base, while

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:25.200
direct rental income faces passive income rules inside a corporation.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:31.300
The pro tip is to compare the after-tax yield net of fees across structures before committing

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:37.200
capital, because a 7% rate yield can drop below a leveraged rental property once financing

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:43.200
costs and vacancy allowances are included. The common misconception is that all real-estate

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:49.100
exposure behaves like owning a home. The fix is to map each option to your account type and time

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:56.520
horizon before allocating. Smart Centers reported second quarter committed occupancy of 98.1%,

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:00.100
with renewed leases showing 6.6% rent growth.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.540
Funds from operations came in at $0.58 per unit,

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:09.080
providing coverage for the current $0.15 monthly distribution.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:13.100
Investors can calculate the units needed for a target income,

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.520
by dividing the annual goal by the distribution per unit,

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.840
and then checking the current price for total capital required.

